  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Greater Value for Gold</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will empower rural communities dependent on artisanal gold mining to advance their own vision of &#x2018;development&#x2019;, by (i)	Developing more favourable commercial partnerships in the gold sector through the establishment of community controlled gold buying hubs, comptoirs, which will invest returns in community development, with particular attention placed on gender equality; (ii)	Gathering knowledge and local voices to inform policy dialogue and legal interventions on artisanal gold mining in Mali, as the political situation allows that; and (iii)	Sharing lessons learned at local, national, regional and international fora through in-person exchange with other artisanal mining communities and highlighting the voices of artisanal miners through blogs, webinars and attendance at key Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) and European Union (EU) mining policy events.The project will equip one community in the Guandiaka commune with a well-functioning central gold buying hub. The office will be located on the main gold mining site and will allow for better control of production and support to combat illegal gold trafficking between the production zone and the neighbouring countries of Guinea and C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire.The revenue from this buying hub will contribute to community and village development in the main site, as well as the satellite sites through exchange and learning as well as advancements to social and health infrastructure.This approach will be shared with three other &#x201c;learning sites&#x201d; where representatives of local artisanal miners will be able to access training to equip them with the knowledge and skills to establish their own buying hubs and potentially replicate the model.</narrative>
  </description>
